      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-168617",
      ":question/problem": "Let $S$ be the boundary of the region. The flux of the vector field $F$ across $S$ represents the rate at which the air passes through the surface. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented, use the divergence theorem to write down the integral that gives this rate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The required rate is ${\u222c}_{S}F\\cdot dS={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$"
